From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Salty <99386653+PjSalty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:42:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] startup: redact credential-bearing values from the env
 dump

Intent: LogEnvironmentInfo prints every JELLYFIN_/DOTNET_/ASPNETCORE_
environment variable with its value at Information on every boot, so a
credential injected as an env var (the acute case: a secretKeyRef named
JELLYFIN_SSO_CLIENT_SECRET) lands in the pod log, the log aggregator,
and every support bundle. The manifest-side fix removes that variable,
but any future JELLYFIN_-prefixed credential would leak the same way.
Keep printing the NAME (it proves the knob is set) and replace the
VALUE with [redacted] whenever the name contains SECRET, PASSWORD,
TOKEN, APIKEY, or API_KEY, matched case-insensitively. Defense in
depth: the manifest change kills the instance, this kills the class.
Carried unchanged onto 12.x (LogEnvironmentInfo is identical; the
setup server still serves the newest log file to local-network clients
during boot, which makes the redaction worth more, not less).
Ceiling: matching is by name only; a secret inside a value whose name
carries none of the markers (a connection string, a URL with
credentials) still prints.
Drop when: upstream redacts its own environment dump.

Patch: 0018
---
 Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs b/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs
index 210832a..e5640f7 100644
--- a/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs
+++ b/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@ public static class StartupHelpers
 {
     private static readonly string[] _relevantEnvVarPrefixes = { "JELLYFIN_", "DOTNET_", "ASPNETCORE_" };
 
+    private static readonly string[] _secretEnvVarMarkers = { "SECRET", "PASSWORD", "TOKEN", "APIKEY", "API_KEY" };
+
     /// <summary>
     /// Logs relevant environment variables and information about the host.
     /// </summary>
@@ -45,9 +47,16 @@ public static class StartupHelpers
         var relevantEnvVars = new Dictionary<object, object>();
         foreach (var key in allEnvVars.Keys)
         {
-            if (_relevantEnvVarPrefixes.Any(prefix => key.ToString()!.StartsWith(prefix, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))
+            var name = key.ToString()!;
+            if (_relevantEnvVarPrefixes.Any(prefix => name.StartsWith(prefix, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))
             {
-                relevantEnvVars.Add(key, allEnvVars[key]!);
+                // A credential-bearing name is still worth listing (it proves the knob
+                // is set), but its value has no business in a log line that ships to
+                // the aggregator and sits in every support bundle.
+                var value = _secretEnvVarMarkers.Any(marker => name.Contains(marker, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
+                    ? "[redacted]"
+                    : allEnvVars[key];
+                relevantEnvVars.Add(key, value!);
             }
         }
 
